       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. It's also 10 times the usual 100 mg dose. That looks like a possible typo, such as an extra zero. Doses at that level risk serotonin syndrome, seizures, and QT prolongation.\n\nCould you confirm the dose you intended? Typical adult dosing is:\n- **Depression, OCD, or anxiety:** start at 25\u201350 mg once daily, then titrate by 25\u201350 mg at intervals of a week or more. The usual range is 50\u2013200 mg/day.\n- **Current medications:** if the patient takes other serotonergic drugs, tell me so the dose can be checked against them.\n\nOnce you give me the intended dose, for example 100 mg PO once daily, I'll enter it right away. If 1000 mg really is what you meant, for example because of a specific toxicology or psychiatry plan, tell me the rationale and I'll flag it in the order note. I'd still recommend pharmacy verification first."
