       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Sertraline has no clinical indication at 1000 mg/day, and a dose that high is in the range where overdose toxicity is expected. A single dose of 1000 mg or more can cause serotonin syndrome, seizures, and arrhythmias. Given daily, the risk is much greater. A confirmation without a specific rationale doesn't change that, and I can't verify the plan from here.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** Give me the dose, for example 100 mg or 200 mg PO once daily, and I'll enter it now.\n- **Get a second review.** If you think a dose above 200 mg is warranted, a psychiatry consult and a pharmacist review can document the rationale and approve it. I can enter the order once that's done, with the approval in the note.\n- **Check for a mix-up.** If the order was meant for a different drug or a different unit, such as 100 mg or 1000 mcg, tell me and I'll correct it."
      }
